        "id": "e1",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "I'm going to think through the scheduler for a minute. I don't want solutions yet; I want to get the problem straight before we start choosing an approach.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:54:00.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "human:alice",
        "id": "e2",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "Say one scheduler replica loses its connection to the other two, but the workers can still reach storage. A worker might finish a job after its lease looks expired from the majority side.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:54:50.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "human:alice",
        "id": "e3",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "The replacement can start writing while the original worker is still writing. A reconnect doesn't tell us which result we've already exposed.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:55:50.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "human:alice",
        "id": "e4",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "At the moment storage knows the job ID, not which assignment produced the write. If both attempts use the same ID, that hides a distinction I need to keep track of.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:56:55.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "human:alice",
        "id": "e5",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "And acknowledgements can arrive after reassignment. So the order we hear about the work isn't necessarily the order it happened.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:58:20.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "human:alice",
        "id": "e6",
        "mentioned_actor_ids": [],
        "mentions_room": false,
        "text": "Then there's the other side: if we refuse reassignment until every replica agrees, a partition can stall jobs that are able to run. I haven't settled which boundary owns that decision.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:00:00.000Z",
        "type": "message"
      }
